{"name":"Strawberry Blonde","hex":"#ffdadc","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"strawberry blonde","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["An uncommon orange hair colour; it is characterized as a combination of pale light yellow (often called blonde) and red. Strawberry blonde hair appears blonde in dim light, but when exposed to sun or a bright light, the hair may assume a slight tinge of pink or red color."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person, especially a woman, who has hair of this colour.","A cocktail comprising one part vodka to two parts cherry brandy to three parts cola topped with a dash of cream and stirred gently with a swizzle stick before serving."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strawberry_blonde"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blond","blocks":[{"text":"Blond or blonde, also referred to as fair hair, is a human hair color characterized by low levels of eumelanin, the dark pigment. The resultant visible hue depends on various factors, but always has some yellowish color. The color can be from the very pale blond to reddish \"strawberry\" blond or golden-brownish (\"sandy\") blond colors. Occasionally, the state of being blond, and specifically the occurrence of blond traits in a predominantly dark or colored population are referred to as blondism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg/330px-Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blond","wikidata":"Q202466"},{"title":"Strawberry Blonde (1980 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Strawberry Blonde (Italian: Bionda fragola is a 1980 Italian film directed by Mino Bellei. It is Bellei's only film as a director. The film is based on the stage play of the same name, which ran for four months at Teatro La Comunita. Mino Bellei and Gianni Felici, who had previously starred in the play, appear in the lead roles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Bionda_fragola_poster_film.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry_Blonde_(1980_film)","wikidata":"Q3640167"},{"title":"Strawberry","blocks":[{"text":"The garden strawberry is a widely grown hybrid plant cultivated worldwide for its fruit. The genus Fragaria, the strawberries, is in the rose family, Rosaceae. The fruit is appreciated for its aroma, bright red colour, juicy texture, and sweetness. It is eaten either fresh or in prepared foods such as jam, ice cream, and chocolates. Artificial strawberry flavourings and aromas are widely used in commercial products. Botanically, the strawberry is not a berry, but an aggregate accessory fruit. Each apparent 'seed' on the outside of the strawberry is actually an achene, a botanical fruit with a seed inside it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg/330px-Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry","wikidata":"Q13158"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg/500px-Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg/1280px-Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg/500px-Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"German footballer Lars Unnerstall, who has blond hair and a blond beard","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALars-Unnerstall2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/500px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/1280px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/500px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of a portrait of Sigismund Casimir Vasa (c. 1644), with characteristic blond hair which darkened with time as confirmed by his later effigies","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_(detail).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Klara_Gadd.jpg/500px-Klara_Gadd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Klara_Gadd.jpg/1280px-Klara_Gadd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Klara_Gadd.jpg/500px-Klara_Gadd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Actress Klara Gadd has strawberry blonde hair","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKlara_Gadd.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Archaeogenetic_analysis_of_human_skin_pigmentation_in_Europe_%28with_Asia_geographic_extension%29.png/500px-Archaeogenetic_analysis_of_human_skin_pigmentation_in_Europe_%28with_Asia_geographic_extension%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par